   "claims": [
    "Learn all you need in 90 seconds with this video we made for you: Watch this on YouTube Overtime – formal definition Almost everybody in the working-age population knows and understands what overtime is.",
    "The most usual rate for overtime hours is time and a half, and that is 50% more than the employee's standard wage.",
    "It means that for every hour of overtime, you receive an equivalent of 1.5 the regular hourly rate.",
    "🙋 Calculate this common 1.5× overtime rate directly with our time and a half calculator.",
    "Multiply the total overtime hours by the answer in 2.",
    "To calculate the monthly overtime pay, follow these steps: Find your overtime pay multiplier say 1.5.",
    "The result is the monthly overtime payment: $93.75.",
    "To find this number: Calculate the product of the overtime monthly hours and the pay multiplier: 10 × 1.5 = 15."
   ],
